Now produce the plan-stage handoff: inspection summary, setup details (none available — everything must be assumed or clarified), proposed approach, assumptions/uncertainties.

I can still propose a concrete design drawing on the canonical OPRO setup (Yang et al. 2023: optimizer LLM proposes candidates based on trajectory of past instructions+scores; BBH full 23/27 tasks; PaLM 2-L as optimizer and PaLM 1/2 family evaluators; 40-example few-shot CoT prompts; etc.) but I must clearly label that as general knowledge, not locally sourced. Also note BBH has 27 tasks (23 main + variants; standard eval uses 23 tasks / 6,511 examples; OPRO paper used full BBH).

